doubao-input (1.1.4-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Tray icon is now Adwaita's monochrome audio-input-microphone-symbolic
    instead of the app's colour logo. The old choice was wrong for a
    16-24px status area: the 256px colourful mark turns to mush at that
    size and does not follow the theme foreground colour, so it looked
    out of place in dark themes. Recording still switches to
    media-record-symbolic (a filled dot). Both are stock Adwaita icons
    present in Adwaita/Yaru/Yaru-dark, with microphone-sensitivity-*
    fallbacks if a trimmed theme dropped them.
  * The app's own logo is unchanged for the settings window, the
    .desktop entry and the app grid.

 -- doubao-input contributors <code-dream@qq.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:35:00 +0800

doubao-input (1.1.3-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Closing the settings window no longer quits the app. Like
    mihomo-manifold, the window is hidden instead and the process keeps
    running with the evdev listener alive; the tray icon is the way back.
    Only "Quit" (tray menu or the Diagnostics page) really exits.
  * The behaviour is gated on the tray actually being shown: the app
    calls Gio.Application.hold() and enables hide-on-close only after
    StatusNotifierWatcher accepts the item. Without a host (stock GNOME
    with no AppIndicator extension) closing the window still quits
    normally, so the app can never end up alive with no way to reach it.
  * Quit releases the hold first, so quit() is not a no-op; shutdown does
    the same for the systemd stop path.
  * Diagnostics: the Quit row now says that closing the window only hides
    it to the tray.

 -- doubao-input contributors <code-dream@qq.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0800

doubao-input (1.1.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Tray icon: the app now exports a real StatusNotifierItem. ui/tray.py
    is implemented in plain Gio/D-Bus (org.kde.StatusNotifierItem on
    /StatusNotifierItem + com.canonical.dbusmenu on /MenuBar) instead of
    libayatana-appindicator, because the only typelib Ubuntu ships is the
    GTK3 one and importing it from a GTK4 process raises ImportError.
    Menu: Show Control Window / Check Microphone / Quit; the icon switches
    to NeedsAttention while recording. Every step degrades silently when
    there is no StatusNotifierWatcher (stock GNOME has none).
  * Fixed: the app did not start at login on Wayland. The unit was
    WantedBy=default.target with After=graphical-session.target, but that
    ordering is inert (graphical-session.target is RefuseManualStart and
    comes up later), so the process started before the Wayland socket
    existed, failed Gtk init and exited 0 - which Restart=on-failure does
    not cover. Now WantedBy=graphical-session.target with an explicit
    After=gnome-session-initialized.target, and the hardcoded
    DISPLAY=:0 is gone. postinst removes the stale
    default.target.wants symlinks left by <=1.1.1.
  * Fixed: the app icon was generic in the shell. The desktop entry is now
    com.doubao.Input.desktop so it matches Gtk.Application's
    application_id (Wayland window app_id), with StartupWMClass for X11.
    Icon switched from an absolute path to the theme name.
  * Icons: ship real per-size PNGs (16..256) instead of one 256x256 SVG
    duplicated into 128x128, plus a -symbolic mic glyph for panels and a
    debian/doubao-input.triggers hook so the icon cache refreshes on
    install instead of at next logout.
  * Diagnostics: report the tray state and, when it is unavailable, say
    which package is missing instead of failing silently.

 -- doubao-input contributors <code-dream@qq.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0800

doubao-input (1.1.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * i18n: the interface is now fully translatable. Source strings are
    English and Chinese comes from gettext catalogs; 1.1.0 shipped a
    half-migrated UI where most of the window was still untranslated,
    so Chinese users saw English labels. zh_CN and zh_TW now cover
    every user-visible string (142 literals + the shortcut/trigger
    option names), including the settings window, first-run wizard,
    shortcut capture, HUD fallback overlay and desktop notifications.
  * Fixed duplicated trigger-key table: doubao/config.py still had the
    Chinese names while ui/control_window.py had the English ones, so
    the settings dropdown and the startup hint disagreed (and the
    English build showed Chinese in the hint). config.py is now the
    single source of truth.
  * Settings: new "Start on login" switch (Input -> Startup). It reads
    the live state from the systemd user unit or the XDG autostart
    entry instead of a cached flag, and flips back with a toast when
    the write fails (no systemd, unwritable ~/.config/autostart).
  * Diagnostics report now lists the autostart state and backend.
  * Autostart module added (systemd user unit + XDG autostart, falls
    back to masking the unit when "systemctl disable" does not stick).

 -- doubao-input contributors <code-dream@qq.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0800

doubao-input (1.1.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Settings: libadwaita three-page PreferencesWindow (账号/输入/诊断).
  * HUD: integrate Myna myna-hud renderer + D-Bus state sync
    (com.canonical.Myna.Dictation), configurable trigger via desktop
    custom shortcuts or evdev physical keys, silence auto-stop,
    first-run onboarding wizard, sounds, diagnostics privacy report.
  * Security hardening:
    - ASR credential file 0600 + config dir 0700 (was world-readable
      0644/0755; cookies are a live account session).
    - Logs no longer contain transcript fragments (length only);
      --log-file accepts bare filenames inside the config dir only.
    - Clipboard cleared 1.5s after successful paste injection.
    - Login WebView: developer extras only under --verbose; login
      detection JS narrowed to the top frame.
    - postinst: version-bounded pip deps; drop unused numpy.
    - systemd user service: NoNewPrivileges/ProtectSystem=full/PrivateTmp.
  * Robustness: evdev partial-event buffering + per-platform
    input_event layout (32-bit); bounded ASR audio backlog (64MB).
  * CI: workflow_dispatch version passed via env (expression-injection
    hardening).
  * UI polish: components moved onto libadwaita defaults — Adw.Banner login
    hint, Gio.Menu hamburger, Adw.ShortcutLabel keycaps, real Adw.Toast,
    wizard navigation moved to a bottom bar.
  * i18n: hamburger gains a Language submenu (English / 简体中文 / 繁體中文,
    stored in settings.json and reapplied on launch); source strings stay in
    English, Chinese provided via gettext .po files.
  * Sounds: reworked so the prompt tones still play when the desktop "Sound"
    switch is off (direct theme-file playback via pw-play/paplay); clipboard
    cleared after injection.
  * Fixed a crash when a desktop shortcut is set (Gtk.accelerator_parse
    arity mismatch in the shortcut-label helper).

 -- doubao-input contributors <code-dream@qq.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0800

doubao-input (1.0.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Logo: replaced white-backed assets with transparent-background
    versions.  Previous logo.png / logo-128.png were RGBA but
    every corner pixel had alpha=255 (opaque white), which made
    the launcher icon look like a square badge and the README
    image show a white frame around the avatar.  The new avatar
    (697×736 RGBA, corners alpha=0) is genuinely transparent so
    the hicolor launcher badge blends with the desktop background
    and the README image sits flush on the page.

 -- doubao-input contributors <code-dream@qq.com>  Sun, 21 Jun 2026 21:50:00 +0800

doubao-input (1.0.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * UI: PttOverlay rounded panel + breathing alpha + glint flash.
    - Rounded 18px corners via CSS provider.
    - Background alpha breathes 0.78~0.98 over 2.4s (opacity, not
      saturation — keeps wallpaper visible without eye strain).
    - Each new ASR word fires a 220ms opacity flash to 1.0 then
      400ms decay back to the breathing baseline.  Causal feedback
      makes the overlay feel alive without ever being noisy.
    - High-contrast white bold text is never animated, so reading
      stays stable while the edge glows.
  * UI: layout bug fixes
    - "你好" was wrapping to 2 lines (one char per line) — locked
      the label to a hard 360px width via set_size_request +
      set_width_chars(14) so Pango has a real break-width before
      the first size allocation.
    - Text appeared shifted right — box changed from HORIZONTAL
      to VERTICAL so the label is centered under the wave, not
      jammed against it.
    - "整行变 …" — removed set_ellipsize(START), which conflicts
      with wrap + max_width_chars + CJK WORD-wrap in GTK 4 /
      Pango and turns the whole line into a single ellipsis.
      Truncation is now handled in Python by text[-600:].
  * Packaging: .desktop Icon= uses absolute path to bypass
    GNOME Shell's per-session icon-theme cache.
  * Packaging: .deb installs wrapper, systemd user service, logo
    to hicolor theme, and postinst bootstraps a per-user venv
    with pure-Python deps (websockets, sounddevice, evdev).

